@startuml
title Cancel appointment

actor Client
participant "NGINX" as NGINX
participant "FE (Next.js)" as FE
participant "BE (Django/DRF)" as BE
database "DB (PostgreSQL)" as DB

Client -> FE : cancel a booked appointment
FE -> NGINX : POST /v1/appointments/{id}/cancel  (X-CSRFToken)
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  AuthN: session; AuthZ: role = client
  appointments.views.AppointmentCancelView
  - ownership check (appointment.client == request.user)
end note
BE -> BE : appointments.services.cancel_appointment(reason=client)
note over BE
  Business rules:
  - not already canceled / completed (made / no_show)
  - self-cancel only up to 24h before start_at;
    within 24h -> contact staff directly (rejected)
  - sets status=canceled, cancel_reason=client
  - reschedules are NOT cancellations (status stays booked)
end note
BE -> DB : UPDATE appointment (status=canceled, cancel_reason)
BE -> BE : notifications.notify_waitlist_for_freed_time()
note right of BE
  If clients are waitlisted for that freed time,
  a BO alert is created for the responsible staff member
  (no automatic offer in v1 — business-rules.md).
end note
BE -> DB : SELECT availability_waitlist ; INSERT notifications_bo_alert
BE --> FE : 200 (AppointmentSerializer, status=canceled)
FE --> Client : cancellation confirmed

note over Client, DB
  Staff cancellation uses /bo/v1/appointments/{id}/cancel
  (reason=staff) and is NOT bound by the 24h cutoff.
end note
@enduml
